":"உடை","lemma":"உடை","gloss":"possess"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"second person singular suffix"}],"gloss":"you possess"},{"surface":"ஆகி","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"become"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"being"},{"surface":"இல்லோர்","parts":[{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"not have"},{"text":"ஓர்","lemma":"ஓர்","gloss":"personal suffix"}],"gloss":"the poor"},{"surface":"கையற","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"அற","lemma":"அறு","gloss":"to be removed"}],"gloss":"so that helplessness is removed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீ","parts":[{"text":"நீ","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"நீடு","parts":[{"text":"நீடு","lemma":"நீடு","gloss":"long time"}],"gloss":"long"},{"surface":"வாழிய","parts":[{"text":"வாழ்","lemma":"வாழ்","gloss":"live"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"optative suffix"}],"gloss":"may you live"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தகை","parts":[{"text":"நெடுந்தகை","lemma":"நெடுந்தகை","gloss":"O noble lord!"}],"gloss":"O noble lord!","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தாழ்நீர்","parts":[{"text":"தாழ்","lemma":"தாழ்","gloss":"deep"},{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"நீர்","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"deep water"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெண்","parts":[{"text":"வெண்","lemma":"வெண்மை","gloss":"white"}],"gloss":"white"},{"surface":"தலைப்","parts":[{"text":"தலைப்","lemma":"தலைப்","gloss":"crested"}],"gloss":"crested","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"புணரி","parts":[{"text":"புணரி","lemma":"புணரி","gloss":"wave"}],"gloss":"waves"},{"surface":"அலைக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"அலைக்கும்","lemma":"அலைக்கும்","gloss":"which beat against"}],"gloss":"which beat against","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செந்தில்","parts":[{"text":"செந்தில்","lemma":"செந்தில்","gloss":"Senthil (Tiruchendur)"}],"gloss":"Senthil"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெடுவேள்","parts":[{"text":"நெடு","lemma":"நெடுமை","gloss":"great"},{"text":"வேள்","lemma":"வேள்","gloss":"Murugan"}],"gloss":"Lord Murugan"},{"surface":"நிலைஇய","parts":[{"text":"நிலை","lemma":"நிலைபெறு","gloss":"reside"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"who resides"},{"surface":"காமர்","parts":[{"text":"காமர்","lemma":"காமர்","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"வியந்துறைக்","parts":[{"text":"வியந்துறைக்","lemma":"வியந்துறைக்","gloss":"wide shore"}],"gloss":"wide shore","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடுவளி","parts":[{"text":"கடு","lemma":"கடுமை","gloss":"fierce"},{"text":"வளி","lemma":"வளி","gloss":"wind"}],"gloss":"fierce wind"},{"surface":"தொகுப்ப","parts":[{"text":"தொகு","lemma":"தொகு","gloss":"gather"},{"text":"ப","lemma":"ப","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to heap up"},{"surface":"ஈண்டிய","parts":[{"text":"ஈண்டு","lemma":"ஈண்டு","gloss":"accumulate"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"accumulated"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வடுஆழ்","parts":[{"text":"வடு","lemma":"வடு","gloss":"scar/depression"},{"text":"ஆழ்","lemma":"ஆழ்","gloss":"deep"}],"gloss":"deep-sinking"},{"surface":"எக்கர்","parts":[{"text":"எக்கர்","lemma":"எக்கர்","gloss":"sand dune"}],"gloss":"sand dunes"},{"surface":"மணலினும்","parts":[{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"மணல்","gloss":"sand"},{"text":"இனும்","lemma":"இனும்","gloss":"than"}],"gloss":"than the sand"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"Rising mountain great bow snake-string having-strung / one arrow having-taken three-fortresses having-destroyed / great strength to-the-gods victory who-gave / stained throat Lord beautiful head-on / crescent-moon forehead shining one-eye like / kings excelled flower-garlanded Maṟaṉ! / fierce angry killer male-elephant-and / swift galloping spirited horse-and / tall banner-bearing lofty chariot-and / courage possessing eager warriors-and thus / four-together excellent although, excellent / righteous-path has-as-its-foundation king's victory / therefore 'our-people' thinking sceptre without-bending / 'others' thinking virtue without-destroying / sun like fierce-power valor-and / moon like cool-great grace-and / sky like generosity-and three / you-possess being poor helplessness-removed / you long may-you-live noble-lord! deep-water / white crested waves beating Senthil / Lord-Murugan who-resides beautiful wide shore / fierce wind to-heap-up accumulated / deep-sinking sand-dunes than-the-sand many-indeed!","translation":"O Maṟaṉ, wearing flower garlands, who excels all other kings! You are like the single eye shining on the forehead with a crescent moon of the Lord with the blue throat, who strung a great snake as a bowstring on the high mountain, shot a single arrow, destroyed the three fortresses, and gave victory to the gods of great strength. Even if a king possesses the fourfold army of fierce, angry killer elephants, swift galloping spirited horses, lofty chariots with tall banners, and brave warriors eager for battle, the victory of his rule is founded on the path of righteousness. Therefore, do not bend your sceptre of justice by favoring your own people, and do not destroy your virtue by treating others harshly. Possessing these three qualities—fierce valor like the sun, cool and great grace like the moon, and boundless generosity like the rain-giving sky—may you, O noble lord, live a long life, removing the helplessness of the poor! May your days of life be more numerous than the sands of the deep-sinking dunes heaped up by fierce winds on the beautiful, wide shore of Senthil, where Lord Murugan resides and where the white-crested waves of the deep sea beat!","modern":"உயர்ந்த மலையாகிய பெரிய வில்லில் பாம்பை நாணாகப் பூட்டி, ஒரு அம்பைக் கொண்டு முப்புரங்களை அழித்து, மிகுந்த வலிமையுடைய தேவர்களுக்கு வெற்றியைத் தந்த, கரிய நஞ்சணிந்த கழுத்தையுடைய சிவபெருமானின் அழகிய தலையில் பிறை நிலவோடு விளங்கும் நெற்றிக்கண் போல, மற்ற அரசர்களை விட மேம்பட்டு விளங்கும் பூமாலை அணிந்த மாறனே! சினம் மிக்க கொலைக் களிறுகளும், விரைந்து பாயும் குதிரைகளும், உயர்ந்த கொடிகளைக் கொண்ட தேர்களும், நெஞ்சுரமும் போர்க்குணமும் கொண்ட வீரர்களும் ஆகிய நான்கு படைகளும் சிறப்பாக அமைந்திருந்தாலும், ஒரு நாட்டின் வெற்றி என்பது அறநெறியை அடிப்படையாகக் கொண்டது. அதனால், 'நம் ஆட்கள்' என்று கருதி உனது செங்கோலை வளைக்காமலும், 'மாற்றார்' என்று கருதி உனது நற்பண்புகளைக் கெடுத்துக் கொள்ளாமலும் ஆட்சி செய்வாயாக. ஞாயிறு போன்ற வெம்மையான ஆண்மையும், திங்கள் போன்ற குளிர்ந்த அருளும், வான் போன்ற கொடையும் ஆகிய இம்மூன்றையும் பெற்று, வறியவர்களின் வறுமையைப் போக்கி, நீ நெடுங்காலம் வாழ்வாயாக! வெண்டலை அலைகள் மோதும் திருச்செந்தூரில், முருகன் எழுந்தருளியிருக்கும் அழகிய கடற்கரையில், கடும் காற்று கூட்டிய பள்ளமான மணல் மேடுகளின் மணல் துகள்களை விடப் பல ஆண்டுகள் நீ வாழ்வாயாக!","explanation":"The poet Madurai Marutan Iḷanākaṉār addresses the Pandyan king Ilavantikaip Paḷḷit Tuñciya Naṉmāṟaṉ in this poem of the Puranaṉuṟu collection. He compares the king's preeminence to the third eye of Lord Shiva, who destroyed the three fortresses of the demons. The poet advises the king that while a powerful fourfold army of elephants, horses, chariots, and warriors is excellent, the true foundation of a king's victory is the path of righteousness. He counsels the king to remain impartial, neither bending the sceptre of justice to favor his own kin nor destroying his virtue when dealing with others. He urges the king to balance fierce valor like the sun, cool grace like the moon, and boundless generosity like the rain-giving sky. Finally, he blesses the king to live a long life, with days more numerous than the sands of the dunes at Senthil, where Lord Murugan resides.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[0.9,1.37],[1.37,1.95],[1.95,2.64],[2.64,3.1],[3.1,3.3],[3.3,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,4.45],[4.6,4.9],[4.9,5.15],[5.15,5.65],[5.65,5.9],[5.9,6.2],[6.2,6.9],[6.9,7.2],[7.2,7.7],[7.7,7.96],[7.96,8.3],[8.3,8.7],[8.7,9.1],[9.1,9.3],[9.3,9.6],[9.6,10.0],[10.0,10.45],[10.45,11.2],[11.2,11.6],[11.6,12.4],[12.